# Security

- Never trust client, worker, or LLM output. Validate types and paths on the server/engine.
- Never hardcode secrets, daemon tokens, or passwords. Do not commit `.env` or MCP bearer tokens.
- Never log PII, tokens, or full unredacted prompts in new telemetry.
- Parameterized SQL only. No shelling out on unvalidated strings.
- Authorization on every mutating or sensitive read. Fail closed (403/deny), not empty-success.
- UI: no unsanitized HTML. React text nodes only for untrusted data.
- Do not weaken the operator tool gate, sandbox, or HITL approval to “make the agent faster.”
- New npm/PyPI deps need a one-line HANDOFF note (why existing code cannot do it). Prefer zero new deps.
